# ti.tm4c123.freertos_demo
# Real, hand-written (no vendor SDK/generator - see target.toml) FreeRTOS
# (CMSIS-RTOS v1) demo for TI Tiva C TM4C123GH6PM - this chip's genuine
# Cortex-M4F core, unlike LM3S6965's Cortex-M3, so the real ARM_CM4F
# FreeRTOS port applies here (already proven by stm32l476/freertos_demo's
# own real, working use of it). See
# ../../../../../replica-server/renoly_examples/ti/tm4c123/README.md.

using sysbus
mach create "TM4C123_FreeRTOS_Demo"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platform.repl

# Bare @$ORIGIN/firmware.elf - REQUIRED, not stylistic, same real reason
# as every other demo's sim.resc in this repo (see blink_uart_demo's own
# sim.resc for the full incident writeup).
sysbus LoadELF @$ORIGIN/firmware.elf

# UART0 DR write watchpoint - observes uartTask's marker/heartbeat bytes.
# is_byte_tap -> Bus Traffic, matching every other UART example.
sysbus AddWatchpointHook 0x4000C000 4 Write "print(chr(value & 0xFF), end='')"

# GPIOF masked-DATA write watchpoint for pin 1 - real, register-level
# proof defaultTask's blink loop genuinely toggles PF1. Not a
# byte-tap -> lands as a real, labeled [GPIOF] Event.
sysbus AddWatchpointHook 0x40025008 4 Write "print('[GPIOF] PF1 write value=0x%X' % (value & 0x2))"

start
